content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22871, on the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-area leakage at approximately one drop per second matches the manual's qualitative symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal'. No numerical allowable leakage rate is documented; the applicable corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 7.6 mm/s at the drive-end bearing housing. Applying the HF-300 bearing-housing vibration zones, defined in mm/s RMS, this exceeds the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary and is within Zone D (7.1-11.0 mm/s): 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. This is the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so SSP-07 requires an immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 84 C. The applicable manufacturer limits are for housing-surface temperature: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is 14 C above the normal maximum and 4 C above the alarm limit, but remains below the 90 C trip limit. Because it exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The approximately 10-minute dry run breached the applicable specification: the HF-300 uses Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and must never run dry. No permissible dry-run duration is given. Dry running is also a documented probable cause of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: worn, cracked or dry-run-damaged mechanical-seal faces following the reported 10-minute dry run, explaining the shaft-area leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment, which is a documented possible contributor to all three principal findings: seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear and/or over-greasing: bearing wear can cause both high vibration and high bearing temperature, while over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation/inadequate NPSH, remains a possible contributor to the high vibration and must be checked during diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately stop P-104 and keep it out of service for repair. Notify the reliability engineer; notification is required before any restart because the vibration is in the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump or working on its seal, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent the pump, and obtain the line-break permit. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-104 is on a chemically dosed filtered-water line.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. Remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; its mass exceeds the 25 kg lifting-control threshold. Use the back pull-out arrangement so the casing and pipework need not be disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the mechanical seal and shaft sleeve in accordance with procedure 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the removed seal faces, sleeve, bearings and impeller. Record wear, cracking, dry-run damage, scoring, imbalance or other damage. Check grease quantity and investigate NPSH/cavitation as possible contributors; do not assume a grease quantity because none is supplied in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Plan replacement of both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Procedure 5.3 requires pair replacement when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature; the reported 84 C high-temperature condition applies. Also complete the grease-quantity and alignment checks required by the troubleshooting table.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Measure shaft-sleeve scoring. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Do not fit seal HF3-450; install one pre-set HF3-450B cartridge seal, for which no sleeve measurement is needed, together with a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten to the applicable torques: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm, using Table 5's lightly-oiled-thread condition. Tighten the M10 HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the superseded 25 Nm manual value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after the seal/bearing work and after any movement of the motor or bearing housing. Meet the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, investigate and correct the cause of the dry run and confirm the Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement from pump discharge; never run the pump dry. Ensure the reliability engineer has been notified before restart. On restart, monitor seal leakage and repeat bearing-housing vibration and housing-surface temperature measurements; stop immediately again if vibration is in Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required in place of HF3-450 for this serial range, with no sleeve measurement needed",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; one of the pair planned for replacement",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing as a pair",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; have one available but fit only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Zone D vibration: stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Work inside the pump or on its seal requires electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is within P-101 to P-106 on the chemically dosed filtered-water line; sodium hypochlorite is present, so chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds 25 kg: use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the specified Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-104 is HF3-22871 and therefore falls within the bulletin range, so HF3-450B governs for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque conflict: manual procedure 5.2 and Table 5 lead to 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because P-104's serial is within the bulletin's range, use 30 Nm; the other unaffected Table 5 torques remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 7.6 mm/s vibration value is RMS, because the Figure 3 zones are specifically defined in mm/s RMS; the fault report does not state RMS (C07).",
    "Confirm that the 84 C temperature was measured on the bearing-housing surface, which is the measurement basis for the manual's temperature limits (C01, C02).",
    "No quantitative acceptable shaft-seal leakage rate or post-repair leakage acceptance criterion is supplied; the troubleshooting document provides only the qualitative leakage symptom and corrective action (C09).",
    "Alignment measurements, grease quantity, bearing and impeller inspection findings, and NPSH/cavitation data are not provided, so the relative contributions of misalignment, bearing wear, over-greasing, impeller damage and cavitation remain unconfirmed (C09).",
    "The evidence says to check grease quantity but gives neither the correct grease type nor quantity; obtain the applicable lubrication specification before adding or changing grease (C09).",
    "Shaft-sleeve scoring depth is unknown until teardown; the decision to fit HF3-455 depends on whether scoring exceeds 0.1 mm (C10, C13).",
    "The cause of the tank-changeover dry run and the current condition/availability of the Plan 11 flush arrangement are not documented and must be established before return to service (C02).",
    "No standard labour allowance is supplied for the additional inspections, NPSH investigation or correction of the dry-run cause; only seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment times are documented (C12)."
  ]
}
